# Every calculation this model makes, at every place it makes it, with a verdict on whether it can
# be made. One row per (site, item examined): which calculation, which layer of which filing,
# whether the operands are there and in one unit, and a sentence saying what is in the way.
#
# Not a check
#   examples/readiness reports this relation, and it answers a different question from
#   checks/all.sqlc. A check says the document contradicts the model. This says a figure cannot be
#   worked out here at all, which is neither a defect in the document nor a pass. Reporting it as a
#   defect accuses a filer of a gap they declared.
#
# Three verdicts, not two
#   `computable`, `suspended` and `not comparable`. A yes-or-no column cannot hold the middle one,
#   and on the corpus it is common: many layers cannot add up their shares because somebody chose
#   not to measure one.
#
# What every site returns
#   One plain SELECT, with no leading WITH, returning exactly `(site, filing, layer, verdict,
#   detail)`, and `verdict` NULL only on the roster row that says a site examined nothing. The
#   checks keep the same shape, for the same reason.
-- arithmetic/roster.sqlc joined to each site's own population.
:union(ALL arithmetic/remainder.sqlc,
           arithmetic/shares_sum.sqlc,
           arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/whole_multiple.sqlc,
           arithmetic/draw_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/exposure_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/time_slack_derived.sqlc,
           arithmetic/filed_remainder.sqlc,
           arithmetic/fusion_sum.sqlc)
